  "Number": 17,
  "Question": "Let \\(f(x)\\) be a function with the two properties:\n\n(a) for any two real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) \\(f(x+y)=x+f(y),\\) and\n\n(b) \\(f(0)=2.\\)\n\nWhat is the value of \\(f(1998)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(1996\\)",
    "D": "\\(1998\\)",
    "E": "\\(2000\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "To use the known value \\(f(0)=2\\), set \\(y=0\\) in property (a). This is allowed because the identity holds for all real inputs. It gives\n\\[\nf(x)=x+f(0)=x+2.\n\\]\nConsequently, \\(f(1998)=1998+2=\\boxed{2000}\\), choice E.",
